---
import { BaseLayout } from "@walle/layouts";
---

<BaseLayout
  headerTitle="Privacy Policy"
  headerDescription="Privacy Policy describing data collection and processing practices."
  headerRobots="noindex, nofollow"
>
  <section class="container prose">
    <h1 style="padding-top: 2rem;">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated: Jul 23, 2026</p>
    <p>
      This notice describes how Fabrizio Cafolla (<a
        href="https://fabriziocafolla.com/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">fabriziocafolla.com</a
      >) processes users' data through the use of TWIPLA (<a
        href="https://twipla.com"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">twipla.com</a
      >) for website analytics. The site collects no other personal data from visitors and has no
      forms.
    </p>

    <h4>1. Data Controller</h4>
    <p>
      The data controller is Fabrizio Cafolla, owner of this blog. For any privacy-related requests,
      you can contact me via LinkedIn.
    </p>

    <h4>2. Data Collected</h4>
    <p>
      TWIPLA is a website analytics service that tracks traffic on our site and collects general
      information from visitors, used to generate statistics that help optimize the visitor
      experience. <strong>We do not use cookies for this process.</strong> TWIPLA may initially process
      technical data (such as truncated IP addresses, operating system, browser type, country) and
      visitor behavior patterns; this data is immediately aggregated and anonymized so that it cannot
      be linked to any specific individual, and is not used to identify visitors or associate them
      with other personal information. Once aggregated, the data is anonymous and no longer
      constitutes personal data under the GDPR. This processing is based on our legitimate interest
      (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR) in monitoring and improving website performance. The site does not use any
      other third-party analytics or tracking tools and has no forms collecting personal data.
    </p>

    <h4>3. Cookies</h4>
    <p>
      The site does not use analytics, profiling, or marketing cookies — TWIPLA does not use cookies.
      Only strictly necessary technical cookies may be used to ensure the site functions correctly.
    </p>

    <h4>4. Users' Rights</h4>
    <p>
      Should you believe any personal data concerning you is being processed through this site, you
      may request access, rectification, or deletion of your data, or object to the analytics
      processing described above, by contacting me via LinkedIn or by using your browser settings to
      block analytics scripts. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Italian Data
      Protection Authority (Garante per la protezione dei dati personali).
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
